### Requests for VS Code REST Client (or PhpStorm's HTTP client)
### Run "login" first; the other requests reuse its token
### Demo users: admin@, planner@, installer1@, installer2@example.com, password "password"

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api

# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "planner@example.com",
    "password": "password"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Current user
GET {{baseUrl}}/user
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List orders (filter + pagination)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?status=in_progress&per_page=5
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "customer_name": "Maryam Rahimi",
    "customer_phone": "09121234567",
    "address": "Tehran, Valiasr St, No. 12"
}

### Order with its jobs
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add a job to an order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/1/jobs
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "title": "Kitchen wall cabinets",
    "installer_id": 3
}

### List jobs (installers only get their own)
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs?status=assembly&per_page=10
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One job
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Move a job to the next stage
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/jobs/1/status
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "status": "cutting"
}

### Status history of a job
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/1/history
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Jobs per stage
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/jobs-per-status
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
